      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T17:20:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is that `rpm_target \u003d\u003d 0` doesn\u0027t mean it\u0027s stopped yet, just that we\u0027re intending for it to be stopped at some point.\n\nLooking at `board_override_fan_control_duty()`, it\u0027s also checking `fan_get_duty(ch) \u003d\u003d 0`, since that\u0027s the actual state of the fan.\n\nSince this test is relying on `fan_test_init()` to reset the duty value, and `fan_test_init()` also resets `rpm_target`, this line should be removed for consistency.",
      "revId": "c2ed0cbb30f294248592d0dd771802382774da09",
